cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the Structural Topology Kernel in research, please cite it as below."
title: "Structural Topology Kernel (STK): deterministic structural coordinates for microstructure images"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Parrish
    given-names: Russell
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0008-9781-7995
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: 2026-10-21
license: MIT
url: https://www.parallaxmetrology.com/stk_pm.html
repository-code: https://github.com/parallaxmetrology/structural-topology-kernel
keywords: [materials informatics, microstructure, SEM, EBSD, featurizer, interpretable descriptors]
abstract: >
  A fixed, training-free 50-coordinate descriptor of grayscale microstructure fields.
  On UHCSDB steel micrographs it reaches 0.832 macro AUC grouped by specimen (HOG 0.728,
  Haralick 0.629), 0.964 on a second bainite dataset, matches standard descriptors on
  2-D permeability, and quantifies label ambiguity. Benchmarks reproduce exactly from
  shipped feature tables.
